      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A Service Holds Data\nAn `aiven_kafka` or `aiven_kafka_connect`\nresource stands for a service: machines, disks\nand the software on them. A change of\n`service_name` or `project` replaces the\nservice. The provider's own docs warn that the\nservice and all its data are deleted before\nAiven creates the new one ([provider warning](\nhttps://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-ai\nven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/index.md#L43-L47)).\n\nThe same page asks you to set\n`termination_protection = true` on every\nproduction service. Aiven itself enforces this\nflag, so it also blocks a delete from the\nconsole or the CLI. It does not protect topics\nor other objects inside the service ([terminat\nion_protection](https://github.com/aiven/terra\nform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/resource\ns/kafka.md#L69)).\n\nThe children of a service, such as topics,\nACLs and connectors, name the service in\n`project` and `service_name`. Those two fields\nforce a replacement on each child too. So a\nreplaced service also replaces everything\ninside it.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-a06a5a1e9089",
      "originalText": "A Service Holds Data\nAn `aiven_kafka` or `aiven_kafka_connect` resource stands for a service: machines, disks and the software on them. A change of `service_name` or `project` replaces the service. The provider's own docs warn that the service and all its data are deleted before Aiven creates the new one ([provider warning](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/index.md#L43-L47)).\n\nThe same page asks you to set `termination_protection = true` on every production service. Aiven itself enforces this flag, so it also blocks a delete from the console or the CLI. It does not protect topics or other objects inside the service ([termination_protection](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/resources/kafka.md#L69)).\n\nThe children of a service, such as topics, ACLs and connectors, name the service in `project` and `service_name`. Those two fields force a replacement on each child too. So a replaced service also replaces everything inside it.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "a-service-holds-data"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
