      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Service Settings Only Grow\nA Kafka service has a block of advanced\nsettings, `kafka_user_config`. It holds broker\ndefaults, the Kafka version, and switches for\nKafka Connect, the Schema Registry and the\nREST proxy. The provider warns: \"There's no\nway to reset advanced configuration options to\ndefault. Options that you add cannot be\nremoved later\" ([kafka_user_config](https://gi\nthub.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v\n4.66.0/docs/resources/kafka.md#L60)).\n\nSo the code shows only the settings that\nsomeone added and kept. A setting that someone\nremoved from the code still runs on the\nservice. To change it, set a new value; to\nlearn the live value, read the service in the\nAiven Console.\n\nBroker defaults in this block also apply to\ntopics. For example,\n`kafka.log_retention_bytes` sets the broker\ndefault for the topic setting\n`retention.bytes`, which every topic without\nits own value uses. That limit counts per\npartition ([Kafka topic settings](https://kafk\na.apache.org/39/generated/topic_config.html)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-5368e92b6534",
      "originalText": "Service Settings Only Grow\nA Kafka service has a block of advanced settings, `kafka_user_config`. It holds broker defaults, the Kafka version, and switches for Kafka Connect, the Schema Registry and the REST proxy. The provider warns: \"There's no way to reset advanced configuration options to default. Options that you add cannot be removed later\" ([kafka_user_config](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/resources/kafka.md#L60)).\n\nSo the code shows only the settings that someone added and kept. A setting that someone removed from the code still runs on the service. To change it, set a new value; to learn the live value, read the service in the Aiven Console.\n\nBroker defaults in this block also apply to topics. For example, `kafka.log_retention_bytes` sets the broker default for the topic setting `retention.bytes`, which every topic without its own value uses. That limit counts per partition ([Kafka topic settings](https://kafka.apache.org/39/generated/topic_config.html)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "service-settings-only-grow"
      }
    },
    {
