      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Topic Name Is the Key\nAn `aiven_kafka_topic` is known by three\nfields: `project`, `service_name` and\n`topic_name`. A change to any of them forces a\nnew topic ([topic fields](https://github.com/a\niven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/doc\ns/resources/kafka_topic.md#L84-L87)). Kafka\ncannot rename a topic, so the old topic and\nits messages are deleted.\n\nThe provider also refuses two changes at plan\ntime ([plan checks](https://github.com/aiven/t\nerraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/internal/\nplugin/service/kafkatopic/topic.go#L161-L186))\n:\n\n- A smaller `partitions` value fails with\n\"number of partitions cannot be decreased\".\n- A new topic resource whose name already\nexists in the service fails with \"topic\nconflict, already exists\".\n\nThe `config` block holds only the topic\nsettings that you set. Removing the block does\nnot reset the topic: it keeps its last values \n([config](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-p\nrovider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/resources/kafk\na_topic.md#L91)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-c2fea1178b0e",
      "originalText": "The Topic Name Is the Key\nAn `aiven_kafka_topic` is known by three fields: `project`, `service_name` and `topic_name`. A change to any of them forces a new topic ([topic fields](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/resources/kafka_topic.md#L84-L87)). Kafka cannot rename a topic, so the old topic and its messages are deleted.\n\nThe provider also refuses two changes at plan time ([plan checks](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/internal/plugin/service/kafkatopic/topic.go#L161-L186)):\n\n- A smaller `partitions` value fails with \"number of partitions cannot be decreased\".\n- A new topic resource whose name already exists in the service fails with \"topic conflict, already exists\".\n\nThe `config` block holds only the topic settings that you set. Removing the block does not reset the topic: it keeps its last values ([config](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/resources/kafka_topic.md#L91)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "the-topic-name-is-the-key"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
