      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Two ACL Models\nAn ACL is an access control list: a rule that\nlets a service user do something. Aiven has\ntwo kinds ([ACLs](https://aiven.io/docs/produc\nts/kafka/concepts/acl)):\n\n- Aiven ACLs, with `aiven_kafka_acl`. Each\ngrants `read`, `write`, `readwrite` or `admin`\non topics. Users and topics can use wildcards.\n- Kafka-native ACLs, with\n`aiven_kafka_native_acl`. They follow Apache\nKafka's own model, with `ALLOW` and `DENY`\nrules on more kinds of resources.\n\nBoth apply at the same time, and a `DENY` rule\nwins over any grant. In Aiven ACLs, `*`\nmatches zero or more characters and `?`\nmatches exactly one. The Schema Registry has\nits own ACLs, in\n`aiven_kafka_schema_registry_acl`.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-ac84019c3524",
      "originalText": "Two ACL Models\nAn ACL is an access control list: a rule that lets a service user do something. Aiven has two kinds ([ACLs](https://aiven.io/docs/products/kafka/concepts/acl)):\n\n- Aiven ACLs, with `aiven_kafka_acl`. Each grants `read`, `write`, `readwrite` or `admin` on topics. Users and topics can use wildcards.\n- Kafka-native ACLs, with `aiven_kafka_native_acl`. They follow Apache Kafka's own model, with `ALLOW` and `DENY` rules on more kinds of resources.\n\nBoth apply at the same time, and a `DENY` rule wins over any grant. In Aiven ACLs, `*` matches zero or more characters and `?` matches exactly one. The Schema Registry has its own ACLs, in `aiven_kafka_schema_registry_acl`.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "two-acl-models"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
