    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8135283785,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-0e9c16f4aea7",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1288.8,
      "y": 1680.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 560.0,
      "seed": 874209,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Two Libraries in One Provider\nThe provider combines two Terraform libraries:\nthe older SDKv2 and the newer Plugin Framework\n(PF). Aiven moves resources to PF one at a\ntime. After a move, a resource stores only the\nvalues that you set, and it drops blocks that\nyour configuration does not have ([upgrade gui\nde](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provide\nr-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/guides/upgrade-guide\n-v3-to-v4.md#L104-L191)). The first plan after\nsuch an upgrade can therefore show changes\nthat remove blocks. Aiven says that applying\nthem is safe.\n\n| Resource | Moved to PF in |\n| --- | --- |\n| `aiven_kafka_schema_registry_acl` | 4.57.0 |\n| `aiven_kafka_topic` | 4.59.0 |\n| `aiven_kafka_acl`, `aiven_kafka_native_acl`,\n`aiven_kafka_user` | 4.61.0 |\n| `aiven_service_integration`,\n`aiven_service_integration_endpoint` | 4.66.0\n|\n\nThe table comes from the [changelog](https://g\nithub.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/\nv4.66.0/CHANGELOG.md). `aiven_kafka`,\n`aiven_kafka_connect`,\n`aiven_kafka_connector`, the schema resources\nand `aiven_project` were still on SDKv2 in\n4.66.0. Each release marks such changes with\n**IMPORTANT** in the changelog.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-0e9c16f4aea7",
      "originalText": "Two Libraries in One Provider\nThe provider combines two Terraform libraries: the older SDKv2 and the newer Plugin Framework (PF). Aiven moves resources to PF one at a time. After a move, a resource stores only the values that you set, and it drops blocks that your configuration does not have ([upgrade guide](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/guides/upgrade-guide-v3-to-v4.md#L104-L191)). The first plan after such an upgrade can therefore show changes that remove blocks. Aiven says that applying them is safe.\n\n| Resource | Moved to PF in |\n| --- | --- |\n| `aiven_kafka_schema_registry_acl` | 4.57.0 |\n| `aiven_kafka_topic` | 4.59.0 |\n| `aiven_kafka_acl`, `aiven_kafka_native_acl`, `aiven_kafka_user` | 4.61.0 |\n| `aiven_service_integration`, `aiven_service_integration_endpoint` | 4.66.0 |\n\nThe table comes from the [changelog](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/CHANGELOG.md). `aiven_kafka`, `aiven_kafka_connect`, `aiven_kafka_connector`, the schema resources and `aiven_project` were still on SDKv2 in 4.66.0. Each release marks such changes with **IMPORTANT** in the changelog.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "two-libraries-in-one-provider"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4379018390,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-bb76505ce05d",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1276.8,
      "y": 1940.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
      "width": 418.8,
      "height": 220.0,
