      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What You Will See\n| Resource | Aiven object | What to check |\nImport ID |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `aiven_project` | project |\n`aiven_organization_project` will replace it\n([project doc](https://github.com/aiven/terraf\norm-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/resources\n/project.md#L11)) | `PROJECT` |\n| `aiven_kafka` | Kafka service |\n`service_name`, `plan`,\n`termination_protection`, `kafka_user_config`\n| `PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME` |\n| `aiven_kafka_connect` | Kafka Connect\nservice | Its integration with the Kafka\nservice | `PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME` |\n| `aiven_service_integration`,\n`aiven_service_integration_endpoint` | link\nbetween services, and an outside target such\nas Prometheus | The type, and secrets in the\nendpoint | `PROJECT/INTEGRATION_ID` |\n| `aiven_kafka_topic` | topic | Name source,\n`partitions`, `replication`, `config` |\n`PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME/TOPIC_NAME` |\n| `aiven_kafka_user` | service user | Password\nand key in state |\n`PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME/USERNAME` |\n| `aiven_kafka_acl`, `aiven_kafka_native_acl`\n| access rule | Wildcard reach; every field\nforces a new rule |\n`PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME/ACL_ID` |\n| `aiven_kafka_schema`,\n`aiven_kafka_schema_configuration` | subject,\nregistry-wide rule | Compatibility level |\n`PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME/SUBJECT` |\n| `aiven_kafka_connector` | connector | Target\nservice, secrets in `config`, stable\n`connector_name` |\n`PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME/CONNECTOR_NAME` |\n\nThe import IDs come from the Import section of\neach [resource doc](https://github.com/aiven/t\nerraform-provider-aiven/tree/v4.66.0/docs/reso\nurces). Aiven generates the ID of an ACL, so\nyou find it in the console or the API before\nan import.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-35bfa397880f",
      "originalText": "What You Will See\n| Resource | Aiven object | What to check | Import ID |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `aiven_project` | project | `aiven_organization_project` will replace it ([project doc](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/docs/resources/project.md#L11)) | `PROJECT` |\n| `aiven_kafka` | Kafka service | `service_name`, `plan`, `termination_protection`, `kafka_user_config` | `PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME` |\n| `aiven_kafka_connect` | Kafka Connect service | Its integration with the Kafka service | `PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME` |\n| `aiven_service_integration`, `aiven_service_integration_endpoint` | link between services, and an outside target such as Prometheus | The type, and secrets in the endpoint | `PROJECT/INTEGRATION_ID` |\n| `aiven_kafka_topic` | topic | Name source, `partitions`, `replication`, `config` | `PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME/TOPIC_NAME` |\n| `aiven_kafka_user` | service user | Password and key in state | `PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME/USERNAME` |\n| `aiven_kafka_acl`, `aiven_kafka_native_acl` | access rule | Wildcard reach; every field forces a new rule | `PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME/ACL_ID` |\n| `aiven_kafka_schema`, `aiven_kafka_schema_configuration` | subject, registry-wide rule | Compatibility level | `PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME/SUBJECT` |\n| `aiven_kafka_connector` | connector | Target service, secrets in `config`, stable `connector_name` | `PROJECT/SERVICE_NAME/CONNECTOR_NAME` |\n\nThe import IDs come from the Import section of each [resource doc](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/tree/v4.66.0/docs/resources). Aiven generates the ID of an ACL, so you find it in the console or the API before an import.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "aiven-what-you-will-see"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
