      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Partition Changes\nRaising `partitions` is an in-place change,\nbut it changes where keys go. The producer\npicks the partition as `hash(key) %\npartitions` ([Kafka partitioner](https://githu\nb.com/apache/kafka/blob/4.1.0/clients/src/main\n/java/org/apache/kafka/clients/producer/intern\nals/BuiltInPartitioner.java#L329-L330)), and\nKafka does not move existing records ([Kafka o\nperations](https://github.com/apache/kafka/blo\nb/b87eb4f673075dc7bb410443689241fcb0302560/doc\ns/operations/basic-kafka-operations.md#L59)).\nThis table uses Kafka's own hash function,\nfrom About the Sources:\n\n| Key | Partition with 3 partitions |\nPartition with 6 partitions |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `truck-17` | 2 | 2 |\n| `truck-42` | 2 | 5 |\n| `truck-88` | 1 | 4 |\n\nAfter the change, new records for `truck-42`\ngo to partition 5, while its older records\nstay in partition 2. A consumer that needs all\nevents of one key in order can then read a\nnewer event before an older one.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-9670ed5dfb6c",
      "originalText": "Partition Changes\nRaising `partitions` is an in-place change, but it changes where keys go. The producer picks the partition as `hash(key) % partitions` ([Kafka partitioner](https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/4.1.0/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/clients/producer/internals/BuiltInPartitioner.java#L329-L330)), and Kafka does not move existing records ([Kafka operations](https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/b87eb4f673075dc7bb410443689241fcb0302560/docs/operations/basic-kafka-operations.md#L59)). This table uses Kafka's own hash function, from About the Sources:\n\n| Key | Partition with 3 partitions | Partition with 6 partitions |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `truck-17` | 2 | 2 |\n| `truck-42` | 2 | 5 |\n| `truck-88` | 1 | 4 |\n\nAfter the change, new records for `truck-42` go to partition 5, while its older records stay in partition 2. A consumer that needs all events of one key in order can then read a newer event before an older one.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "partition-changes"
      }
    },
