      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Secrets in Connector Config\nThe provider stopped marking connector\n`config` as sensitive in 4.2.0 ([changelog](ht\ntps://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aive\nn/blob/v4.66.0/CHANGELOG.md#L1399)). A plan\nprints each value that does not come from a\nsensitive variable, and the state stores every\nvalue in plain text. In Aiven, any user with\n`service:data:write` can read connector\nconfigurations, which \"can contain secrets in\nplain text\" ([permissions](https://aiven.io/do\ncs/platform/concepts/permissions)). Kafka\nConnect secret providers keep the value out:\nthe config holds a reference to AWS Secrets\nManager instead ([secret providers](https://ai\nven.io/docs/products/kafka/kafka-connect/howto\n/configure-secret-providers)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-862386f375a4",
      "originalText": "Secrets in Connector Config\nThe provider stopped marking connector `config` as sensitive in 4.2.0 ([changelog](https://github.com/aiven/terraform-provider-aiven/blob/v4.66.0/CHANGELOG.md#L1399)). A plan prints each value that does not come from a sensitive variable, and the state stores every value in plain text. In Aiven, any user with `service:data:write` can read connector configurations, which \"can contain secrets in plain text\" ([permissions](https://aiven.io/docs/platform/concepts/permissions)). Kafka Connect secret providers keep the value out: the config holds a reference to AWS Secrets Manager instead ([secret providers](https://aiven.io/docs/products/kafka/kafka-connect/howto/configure-secret-providers)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "secrets-in-connector-config"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
