    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2572851341,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-44344e6522c3",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1879.6000000000001,
      "y": 4259.0,
      "strokeColor": "#92400E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 420.0,
      "seed": 32347,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Keys That Kafka Connect Ignores\nThe provider accepts any key, and Kafka's\nconfig classes only log unused keys at info\nlevel ([AbstractConfig](https://github.com/apa\nche/kafka/blob/4.1.0/clients/src/main/java/org\n/apache/kafka/common/config/AbstractConfig.jav\na#L386-L391)). So a misplaced setting does\nnothing, and no error says so. Two examples:\n\n- A consumer setting for one connector needs\nthe prefix `consumer.override.`, for example\n`consumer.override.max.poll.records` ([Kafka\nConnect user guide](https://github.com/apache/\nkafka/blob/b87eb4f673075dc7bb410443689241fcb03\n02560/docs/kafka-connect/user-guide.md#L57)).\n- `offset.flush.interval.ms` is a worker\nsetting. It is not a connector setting\n([worker settings](https://kafka.apache.org/39\n/generated/connect_config.html)).\n\nAiven also says that `plugin_version` inside a\nconnector config has no effect ([connector ver\nsions](https://aiven.io/docs/products/kafka/ka\nfka-connect/howto/manage-connector-versions)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-44344e6522c3",
      "originalText": "Keys That Kafka Connect Ignores\nThe provider accepts any key, and Kafka's config classes only log unused keys at info level ([AbstractConfig](https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/4.1.0/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/common/config/AbstractConfig.java#L386-L391)). So a misplaced setting does nothing, and no error says so. Two examples:\n\n- A consumer setting for one connector needs the prefix `consumer.override.`, for example `consumer.override.max.poll.records` ([Kafka Connect user guide](https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/b87eb4f673075dc7bb410443689241fcb0302560/docs/kafka-connect/user-guide.md#L57)).\n- `offset.flush.interval.ms` is a worker setting. It is not a connector setting ([worker settings](https://kafka.apache.org/39/generated/connect_config.html)).\n\nAiven also says that `plugin_version` inside a connector config has no effect ([connector versions](https://aiven.io/docs/products/kafka/kafka-connect/howto/manage-connector-versions)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "keys-that-connect-ignores"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4395952925,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-4a432a5b72c4",
