    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 7576690908,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-9a537d2af2ee",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1321.2,
      "y": 6871.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 175.0,
      "seed": 400814,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Secret References over Secret Values\nA connector config can hold a secret value, or\na reference that Kafka Connect resolves at run\ntime from AWS Secrets Manager or from\nenvironment variables ([secret providers](http\ns://aiven.io/docs/products/kafka/kafka-connect\n/howto/configure-secret-providers)). The\nreference keeps the secret out of the state,\nthe plan and the connector API. It costs one\nmore setup step on the Connect service.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-9a537d2af2ee",
      "originalText": "Secret References over Secret Values\nA connector config can hold a secret value, or a reference that Kafka Connect resolves at run time from AWS Secrets Manager or from environment variables ([secret providers](https://aiven.io/docs/products/kafka/kafka-connect/howto/configure-secret-providers)). The reference keeps the secret out of the state, the plan and the connector API. It costs one more setup step on the Connect service.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "secret-references"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 7885523018,
