    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 6878898072,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-8ee2140372f2",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 730.0,
      "y": 7597.0,
      "strokeColor": "#57534E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 397.8,
      "height": 877.5,
      "seed": 508701,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "About the Sources\nThe provider facts come from the `aiven/aiven`\nrepository at tag v4.66.0, the latest release on\n2026-11-23. The Aiven facts come from aiven.io/docs\non the same day.\n\nThe partition table comes from this Python script.\nIt copies Kafka's `murmur2` function and its\ndefault partitioner, and it checks itself against\nthree test values from Kafka's own tests ([UtilsTes\nt](https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/4.1.0/clien\nts/src/test/java/org/apache/kafka/common/utils/Util\nsTest.java#L106-L118)):\n\n```python\ndef murmur2(data: bytes) -> int:\nlength = len(data)\nm, r = 0x5BD1E995, 24\nh = (0x9747B28C ^ length) & 0xFFFFFFFF\nfor i in range(length // 4):\ni4 = i * 4\nk = data[i4] | data[i4 + 1] << 8 | data[i4 + 2] <<\n16 | data[i4 + 3] << 24\nk = (k * m) & 0xFFFFFFFF\nk ^= k >> r\nk = (k * m) & 0xFFFFFFFF\nh = (h * m) & 0xFFFFFFFF\nh ^= k\nrest = length % 4\nif rest == 3:\nh ^= data[(length & ~3) + 2] << 16\nif rest >= 2:\nh ^= data[(length & ~3) + 1] << 8\nif rest >= 1:\nh ^= data[length & ~3]\nh = (h * m) & 0xFFFFFFFF\nh ^= h >> 13\nh = (h * m) & 0xFFFFFFFF\nh ^= h >> 15\nreturn h - (1 << 32) if h & 0x80000000 else h\n\n\ndef partition(key: str, partitions: int) -> int:\nreturn (murmur2(key.encode()) & 0x7FFFFFFF) %\npartitions\n\n\nassert murmur2(b\"21\") == -973932308\nassert murmur2(b\"foobar\") == -790332482\nassert murmur2(b\"a-little-bit-long-string\") ==\n-985981536\nfor key in [\"truck-17\", \"truck-42\", \"truck-88\"]:\nprint(key, partition(key, 3), partition(key, 6))\n```",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 16.25,
      "containerId": "node-8ee2140372f2",
      "originalText": "About the Sources\nThe provider facts come from the `aiven/aiven` repository at tag v4.66.0, the latest release on 2026-11-23. The Aiven facts come from aiven.io/docs on the same day.\n\nThe partition table comes from this Python script. It copies Kafka's `murmur2` function and its default partitioner, and it checks itself against three test values from Kafka's own tests ([UtilsTest](https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/4.1.0/clients/src/test/java/org/apache/kafka/common/utils/UtilsTest.java#L106-L118)):\n\n```python\ndef murmur2(data: bytes) -> int:\n    length = len(data)\n    m, r = 0x5BD1E995, 24\n    h = (0x9747B28C ^ length) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    for i in range(length // 4):\n        i4 = i * 4\n        k = data[i4] | data[i4 + 1] << 8 | data[i4 + 2] << 16 | data[i4 + 3] << 24\n        k = (k * m) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n        k ^= k >> r\n        k = (k * m) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n        h = (h * m) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n        h ^= k\n    rest = length % 4\n    if rest == 3:\n        h ^= data[(length & ~3) + 2] << 16\n    if rest >= 2:\n        h ^= data[(length & ~3) + 1] << 8\n    if rest >= 1:\n        h ^= data[length & ~3]\n        h = (h * m) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    h ^= h >> 13\n    h = (h * m) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    h ^= h >> 15\n    return h - (1 << 32) if h & 0x80000000 else h\n\n\ndef partition(key: str, partitions: int) -> int:\n    return (murmur2(key.encode()) & 0x7FFFFFFF) % partitions\n\n\nassert murmur2(b\"21\") == -973932308\nassert murmur2(b\"foobar\") == -790332482\nassert murmur2(b\"a-little-bit-long-string\") == -985981536\nfor key in [\"truck-17\", \"truck-42\", \"truck-88\"]:\n    print(key, partition(key, 3), partition(key, 6))\n```",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "aiven-about-the-sources"
      }
    },
